<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Federal Dora     arrived     barley	    9,900     U.S.</p>
<p>				     wheat	     5,690</p>
<p>				     wheat	     9,620</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	arrived     wheat	    36,257     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya		2,499</p>
<p>				     corn	     22,500</p>
<p>Halilaga	   arrived     maize grits     2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Tonglacky	  26/12	 maize grits     2,700     Europe</p>
<p>Ivonne	     28/12	 corn		4,123     Europe</p>
<p>Fany		 29/12	 corn	     21,733     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya		8,976</p>
<p>				     wheat	     9,081</p>
<p>Unity		01/01	 sorghum	  10,500     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn	     22,000</p>
<p>				     corn-gluten    11,300</p>
<p>				     corn-screening  6,500</p>
<p>Chupa 02/01	 wheat	     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Auk		  03/01	 sorghum	  21,365     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     13,000</p>
<p>Sac Malaga	 08/01	 barley	   25,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Laketahoy	  10/01	 barley	   20,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Solidarnosk	15/01	 n/a		60,000     U.S.</p>
</text>
